 So larger plans do better, up to the point where they hit spoilage and the 152-unit storage limit; candidate 2 is close to it.\n- Expected order within this group: 0 ≈ 2 > 3 > 1 > 4.\n\n**Candidate 7.** The day-5 order (126 units for days 10–11) is cancelled because cash is negative. The day-7 order is only slightly cut back. Overall it loses fewer units than candidates 0–4 (about 150 against about 220), so I put it in the better half.\n\n**Candidate 6 (every 3 days, large batches).** The day-3 order is partly cut back and the day-6 order (146 units) is cancelled. This leaves a long gap in product 1 on days 9–13. Large deliveries also risk going over the storage limit.\n\n**Candidate 5 (orders every day).** It pays the 54 fee 25 times, about 650 more than the others. Cash shortages cascade: the day-4 order is cut back, the day-5 order is cancelled, and the day-6 order is cut back again."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5054, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5054}, "output_tokens": 7, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T09:25:12.803Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWHX4dC1HoU7hThh5xbz"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Goh2QrEfVSc1GHgxZnuSyb", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWHX4sa5Gkh1rxi9rqRn", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_u